# What this repository's release needs that another's does not. See propensive/.github, which
# holds the script; a release is cut by `git tag -s xek-X.Y && git push --tags`.
#
# xek releases no jars: a release is the five native runner stubs, the `xek` builder script (also
# as `xek.cmd`) and their checksums, assembled by etc/ci/runners-assemble.sh rather than by Mill's
# `release.stage`. The shared script gates, uploads, verifies every digest, writes the notes and
# rolls back exactly as it does for the jars of the other repositories.

name       xek
title      xek

# Tags are `xek-<version>`. Those before the rename, `xeq-<version>`, are earlier releases too, so
# the notes of the first `xek-` release start from the last `xeq-` one.
tag        xek- xeq-

assemble   ./etc/ci/runners-assemble.sh

# The hashes just published go into etc/runners/ and res/packager/xek/, in a pull request here.
after      ./etc/ci/runners-record.sh
